---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Constellation from "../components/Constellation.astro";
import { site, href } from "../data/site";
import { clusters, coverage } from "../data/clusters";
import { leadership, smallN, limit, ladder } from "../data/parsimony";
import { operators, typedEdge } from "../data/contracts";
import { filled, open } from "../data/gaps";
import { scorePath, edges } from "../data/graph";
import { dataHub } from "../data/members";

// short, grounded action phrase per pipeline step (the ORCHESTRA.md app chain)
const action: Record<string, string> = {
  masque: "Build a synthetic copy of the private data that keeps the link between treatment and outcome, and develop the analysis on it.",
  PESTO: "Calibrate the crop simulator to the field: work backwards from the measurements to the settings that reproduce them, running many versions to show the uncertainty.",
  proxymix: "Summarise the range of plausible settings as a simple mix of bell curves that the next test can use.",
  kernR: "Test whether the effect agrees with how the crop works, not only with the measured outcome (TACI, a method in development).",
  decideR: "Choose the action that weighs what a wrong call costs and allows for risk, or refuse if any input has not been checked.",
  grainPlan: "Turn the decision into a grain plan: nitrogen rate, variety, grade target, season.",
};
// presentation split of the grounded tagline — reconstructs it byte-identical
const [tagPre, tagPost] = site.tagline.split(", not ");
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "WebSite",
  name: site.name, description: site.intro,
  author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Max Moldovan", identifier: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9680-8474" },
};
---
<Base title="Home" description={site.intro} path="/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-in">
      <p class="kicker">Crop analytics · {site.counts.members} R packages · {site.counts.contracts} contracts</p>
      <h1 class="hero-h1">{tagPre}, <em>not</em> {tagPost}</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-3">{site.intro}</p>
      <div class="hero-stats">
        <div class="hs"><span class="n" data-count={site.counts.members}>{site.counts.members}</span><span class="l">R packages</span></div>
        <div class="hs"><span class="n" data-count={site.counts.contracts}>{site.counts.contracts}</span><span class="l">contracts (agreed hand-over formats)</span></div>
        <div class="hs"><span class="n" data-count={edges.length}>{edges.length}</span><span class="l">links between packages</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4"><Constellation /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap reveal">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">The thesis</p>
      <h2>Composition, <em>not</em> consolidation</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="prose lead">Most analytics platforms grow by absorbing everything into one
      large program. The orchestra does the opposite: many small packages, each doing one
      job well. Every package writes its results in <em>one</em> shared record, the
      manifest (<code>orchestra_manifest</code>), and passes them on through {site.counts.contracts}
      contracts, agreed formats for handing a result from one package to the next. The
      software that runs a study stops when a result arrives in the wrong form, and
      abstains, meaning it declines to answer and says why, when there is too little
      evidence.</p>
    <p class="prose muted mt-3">{typedEdge}</p>
    <p class="prose mt-3"><strong>{dataHub.id}</strong> is the data layer underneath the
      packages; it is not an R package. It holds {dataHub.nDatasets} open datasets,{" "}
      {dataHub.nAustralia} of them Australian, each recorded with its source and licence
      and indexed by the questions it can answer, so a study can find the data it needs.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band"><div class="wrap reveal" id="pipeline">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">How a study runs</p>
      <h2>From a synthetic copy of the data to a checked decision</h2>
      <p class="prose muted mt-2">One real chain of steps, end to end. Each step is done by
        one package; the software checks every hand-over between two packages, and two
        further checks can stop a branch or reconcile conflicting answers before any
        decision is issued.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pipe" data-stagger>
      {scorePath.map((id, i) => (
        <div class="pstep">
          <div class="pn">step {i + 1} of {scorePath.length}</div>
          <div class="pid">{id}</div>
          <div class="pd">{action[id]}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="prose muted small mt-3">Between the steps, the first check stops a branch when
      there is too little evidence. The second compares answers from independent methods:
      when they agree, each supports the other; when they split, the split is flagged. A
      result in the wrong form stops the run rather than being quietly converted.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wrap reveal" id="clusters">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Kinds of problem</p>
      <h2>What it solves, and which package leads</h2>
      <p class="prose muted mt-2">Every question is described by two things: the kind of
        response measured and the structure of the model. Questions fall into a few tasks,
        each led by one package; the explorer at the top of the page shows exactly which
        packages each task uses.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="matrix" data-stagger>
      {clusters.map((c) => (
        <div class="cl">
          <div class="task">{c.task}</div>
          <div class="lead">lead · {c.lead} · {c.members.length} tool{c.members.length > 1 ? "s" : ""}</div>
          <p>{c.blurb}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="prose muted small mt-3">Kinds of response covered: {coverage.families.join(", ")}.
      Model structures covered: {coverage.structures.join(", ")}. {coverage.note}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap reveal" id="parsimony">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">As few tools as needed</p>
      <h2>One tool when one is enough. Many when needed. <em>Never</em> more.</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="takeaway">Studies use several packages <em>by design</em>: each lead package
      works with at least three packages, so no result rests on a single method. Just as
      important, the system <strong>abstains</strong> rather than claim more than the
      evidence supports.</p>
    <p class="explore-lbl mt-3">Packages each lead package works with</p>
    <div class="lead-cards" data-stagger>
      {leadership.map((l) => (<div class="lc"><div class="n" data-count={l.members}>{l.members}</div><div class="who">{l.lead}</div></div>))}
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll mt-3">
      <table class="num">
        <caption>Test with very few observations (N): the share of results that were confident but wrong (lower is better). The calibrated design, synthetic control, declines to answer; the other two stay confident.</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>design</th>{smallN.cols.map((c) => <th>{c}</th>)}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>{smallN.rows.map((r) => (<tr><td>{r.design}</td>{r.cells.map((c) => <td>{c}</td>)}<td>{r.abstains}</td></tr>))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="prose muted mt-3">{limit}</p>
    <p class="prose muted mt-2">{ladder}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band"><div class="wrap reveal" id="disciplines">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Two built-in checks</p>
      <h2>Decline when unsure, and compare independent answers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2" data-stagger>
      {operators.map((op) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3><code>{op.name}</code></h3>
          <p class="muted mt-2">{op.what}</p>
          <p class="small mt-3"><span class="badge">when</span> {op.when}</p>
          <p class="small mt-2"><span class="badge">modes</span> {op.modes}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="wrap reveal" id="gaps">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">Gaps</p>
      <h2>What is not covered yet: filled where a tool has been checked, open where not</h2>
      <p class="prose muted mt-2">The orchestra lists its own gaps. Where a strong outside tool
        exists, it names the one the orchestra would call, with the licence condition that
        matters. Where no tool has passed checking yet, it says so: the same rule of declining
        to answer, applied to itself.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="explore-lbl">Filled: a checked outside tool the orchestra can call</p>
    <div class="gaps" data-stagger>
      {filled.map((g) => (
        <div class="gap filled">
          <h3>{g.gap}</h3>
          <p class="use">{g.use}</p>
          <p class="tool">→ {g.tool}</p>
          <p class="lic">licence · {g.licence}</p>
          <p class="use mt-2">{g.caveat}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="explore-lbl mt-3">Open: no tool checked yet</p>
    <div class="gaps" data-stagger>
      {open.map((g) => (
        <div class="gap open">
          <h3>{g.gap}</h3>
          <p class="use">{g.use}</p>
          <p class="use mt-2">{g.note}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="cta-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href={href("/members")}>The full catalogue</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={href("/about")}>Why it's built this way</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
